1
00:00:03,862 --> 00:00:07,145
[SPEAKER_02]: Was he pleasant at all with you?

2
00:00:07,205 --> 00:00:08,366
[SPEAKER_02]: Could he be pleasant?

3
00:00:10,007 --> 00:00:12,209
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh yes, he could be a perfect gentleman.

4
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:16,033
[SPEAKER_00]: He was perfectly mannered.

5
00:00:16,233 --> 00:00:22,959
[SPEAKER_00]: The situation eventually came up, I let my little finger stick out when I threw my change of pace.

6
00:00:27,614 --> 00:00:29,495
[SPEAKER_00]: It was a dead giveaway to smart batters.

7
00:00:29,575 --> 00:00:34,278
[SPEAKER_00]: Next time he pitched against Detroit, I said to him before he went to mound, now wait when Cobb comes up and shit.

8
00:00:34,758 --> 00:00:36,379
[SPEAKER_00]: Situation called that knuckle of his.

9
00:00:36,579 --> 00:00:38,320
[SPEAKER_00]: He never said anything of the East kind.

10
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:43,282
[SPEAKER_00]: I want you to let your little finger stick out just as if you're going to throw the knuckle, but don't throw it.

11
00:00:43,803 --> 00:00:45,204
[SPEAKER_00]: He never told me anything of the kind.

12
00:00:45,324 --> 00:00:46,164
[SPEAKER_00]: I did these things.

13
00:00:46,204 --> 00:00:47,685
[SPEAKER_00]: I learned all these things myself.

14
00:00:48,145 --> 00:00:53,348
[SPEAKER_00]: What I want you to do is aim your pitch at the center of Cobb's forward and throw that ball just as hard as you can.

15
00:00:54,327 --> 00:00:55,627
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, don't worry about hitting him.

16
00:00:55,667 --> 00:00:57,208
[SPEAKER_00]: He's got the best eyes in the league.

17
00:00:57,228 --> 00:01:00,588
[SPEAKER_00]: Pitchers have been throwing at his head for 15 years, and nobody's hit it yet.

18
00:01:01,388 --> 00:01:02,368
[SPEAKER_00]: So continued Cobb.

19
00:01:02,388 --> 00:01:06,809
[SPEAKER_00]: When the situation came up, Waite let his little fingers stick out so Cobb could see it.

20
00:01:07,309 --> 00:01:08,610
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he decked him, but good.

21
00:01:08,650 --> 00:01:11,130
[SPEAKER_00]: And the dust really flew at the home plate.

