[SPEAKER_00]: When Waite did the same thing and decked him a second time, Cobb just sat there on the ground, smoothing

24
00:01:23,523 --> 00:01:28,408
[SPEAKER_00]: the day with the palm of his hand, and suddenly looked out at Hoyt and hollered, you must be rooming with Mays.

25
00:01:28,988 --> 00:01:32,171
[SPEAKER_00]: You must be rooming with Mays.

26
00:01:33,192 --> 00:01:34,072
[SPEAKER_02]: That's a good story.

27
00:01:34,413 --> 00:01:39,397
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a good story, but every damn word, and it's a lie, you see.

28
00:01:40,398 --> 00:01:41,859
[SPEAKER_00]: Nothing like that ever took place.

29
00:01:42,419 --> 00:01:44,341
[SPEAKER_00]: Where he gets those ideas, I don't know.

30
00:01:44,441 --> 00:01:46,203
[SPEAKER_00]: He just got old.

31
00:01:50,081 --> 00:02:01,548
[SPEAKER_00]: He was a great pitcher there, there's no doubt about it, and if he had paid... More happened to Carl, it strikes me that when a fellow...

32
00:02:02,569 --> 00:02:13,596
[SPEAKER_00]: When a fellow becomes beset... Well, that's the wrong way to start this thought, anyway.

